# CLAUDE.local.md — private overlay

**Gitignored.** Project-private supplement to `CLAUDE.md`. Claude
Code auto-loads this; the public repo never sees it. Workspace backup:
`tick-trader-percore-workspace/CLAUDE.local.md.backup` via
`/sync-workspace`.

**This file is an INDEX.** Each rule = one-line statement + one-line
trigger + canonical-doc pointer. Deep-dive bodies (Why + How to
apply + worked examples + anti-patterns) live in:

- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DESIGN_SPECS/<pattern>.md` — pattern bodies
- `DOCS/RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md` — bug class registry
- `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md`, `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md`, `FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` — auto-write ledgers
- `~/.claude/projects/-home-caramel-code-FoxML-Trader-v2/memory/` — feedback / user / project memories
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/claude-skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` — operational contracts
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/LANDMINES.md` — operational pitfalls
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` — thematic narrative + 4-tier discipline classification + cross-reference index; the WHY companion to `CLAUDE.md`
- `CLAUDE.md` — slimmed to operational orientation + H1-H20 hard invariants + reference table (always loaded)

Skills that fire on relevant work load matching DESIGN_SPECS bodies
dynamically — see "Skill load contracts" below.

---

## Required reading before performance-sensitive code

| Doc | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `DOCS/STRATEGY_AND_CODING_RULES.md` | any code in hot path, slow path, OMS drainer, parsing, ML inference, strategies. 11 strict invariants. |
| `DOCS/LATENCY_OPTIMIZATION_AUDIT.md` | any optimization investigation, performance-regression triage. 13 parts. |
| `plans/_cross-cutting/2026-05-06-latency-path-discipline.md` | any modification to latency-impacting path. 7 architectural rules scaled by cadence + anti-pattern history + pre-merge checklist. |
| `DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` | cold-pickup of unfamiliar surface; designing non-trivial change; cross-family trade-off; new pattern codification. 14 sections with cross-ref index. |

Workflow: rules doc first → audit doc for "yes but how" → hot-path
discipline when touching per-tick code → philosophy doc when
designing rather than implementing.

